# Explore video briefs

New `videos/*.mp4` files are not live until they are renamed and added as curated stories in `data.json`. Do not leave raw uploads unlinked.

## Ingest checklist

1. Rename to `videos/[a-z0-9-]+.mp4`. `index.html` `safeMediaPath` only accepts `videos/[\w./-]+`, so spaces, punctuation and emoji will not play.
2. Skip duplicates (same size/content as an existing clip). Do not add a second card.
3. Insert a curated story next to the other video briefs (before `paul-and-mike-indian-chocolate` unless a better neighbour is obvious).
4. Match this shape and voice — editorial headline, no clickbait, no emoji, no raw filename as the title:

```json
{
  "id": "short-kebab-id",
  "material": "Neem",
  "region": "India",
  "headline": "Declarative sentence naming the opportunity",
  "dek": "One sentence on the commercial idea.",
  "potential_score": 4,
  "potential_label": "High — short market reason",
  "capital_note": "Low/mid/high: what the money buys",
  "video": "videos/short-kebab-id.mp4",
  "video_caption": "What the clip shows",
  "body": "2–4 sentences: the uploaded brief, the value chain, and the commercial catch.",
  "why_it_matters": "One sentence on why this is a business signal.",
  "sources": [{ "name": "Watch uploaded brief", "url": "videos/short-kebab-id.mp4" }]
}
```

5. Identify the company or process when the clip is specific (e.g. BioCap, Malai). Add a named source URL if known.
6. Auto-RSS entries (`why_it_matters` starting `Auto-generated entry`) are a different format. Do not use that for uploaded videos.
